WEBVTT

01:23.250 --> 01:24.720
Emergency!

02:04.970 --> 02:07.930
What?
What the hell is going on?

02:08.510 --> 02:10.590
Anomaly in the sub-space room!

02:10.720 --> 02:14.340
Conventional space/time is being
drawn into the core block.

02:14.420 --> 02:15.760
Commander, could this be...?

02:15.930 --> 02:17.250
It's him!

02:17.380 --> 02:20.490
The only one who could do
something like this is him!

02:24.250 --> 02:25.720
The time axis is
out of alignment.

02:25.800 --> 02:29.420
It's slipped into negative!
Time and space is moving past!

02:29.510 --> 02:31.380
Time and space is moving?

02:31.460 --> 02:34.090
Commander! The sub-space
anomaly is growing fast!

02:34.210 --> 02:36.210
At this rate, the whole
Galaxy Police will be...

02:37.930 --> 02:39.090
Commander!

03:37.760 --> 03:39.170
It's from Headquarters.

03:39.300 --> 03:41.930
Oh, they just want
our regular report again!

03:42.670 --> 03:44.630
<i>Attention to all GP units.</i>

03:44.720 --> 03:47.630
<i>Kain, who's been in custody,</i>
<i>has escaped...</i>

03:49.010 --> 03:51.420
Look what you've done.
You've wasted all those snacks.

03:51.510 --> 03:53.590
Headquarters,
can you come in, please?

03:53.670 --> 03:56.800
This is Detective First
Class Kiyone, Solar System.

03:56.880 --> 03:57.970
Come in, please!

04:00.050 --> 04:02.510
Come in, please.

04:02.630 --> 04:06.670
Headquarters? Headquarters?
Come in, please!

04:16.090 --> 04:18.050
What's the matter?
What has happened?

04:34.720 --> 04:36.970
Hey, look at that!
That's the aurora borealis!

04:37.050 --> 04:40.880
Yeah, it is! But I never thought
it could be seen here in Tokyo.

05:09.630 --> 05:13.590
<i>This was a warning</i>
<i>that I was going to vanish.</i>

05:25.090 --> 05:32.250
AUTUMN 1970

09:07.340 --> 09:09.010
8mm camera?

09:09.130 --> 09:11.840
Yep. It's a camera for people
to make their own movies.

09:11.970 --> 09:13.170
Hmm.

09:14.130 --> 09:18.130
My father was always crazy
about gadgets like this.

09:18.840 --> 09:22.340
This is a film
he shot years ago.

09:29.090 --> 09:32.760
It was pretty sneaky way
of Dad to pick up my Mom.

09:33.090 --> 09:36.630
What? You mean that girl
is your mother?

09:37.010 --> 09:38.300
Mm-hmm.

09:39.840 --> 09:41.670
Wow, is she ever young!

09:41.800 --> 09:43.130
Sure, she is!

09:43.210 --> 09:45.880
She was in
high school then.

09:46.010 --> 09:46.880
Excuse me!

09:51.720 --> 09:52.880
She's so pretty!

09:53.170 --> 09:54.550
Of course she is.

09:54.720 --> 09:59.210
Tenchi's mother is descended
from the Jurai royal family.

09:59.300 --> 10:03.460
That's weird. You've got
Jurai blood, too, don't you?

10:03.550 --> 10:04.550
And just what
does that mean?

10:04.670 --> 10:07.550
Hey! What're you doing?

10:07.630 --> 10:09.380
You can't have them all!

10:09.510 --> 10:11.380
Hmph! I won't waste
these crackers on you!

10:11.510 --> 10:13.550
But they're not yours
to begin with.

10:14.170 --> 10:15.880
She looks so gentle.

10:16.050 --> 10:17.010
Mmm.

10:36.670 --> 10:38.840
My-my body is...

10:43.550 --> 10:45.090
Tenchi! What's going on?

10:45.250 --> 10:46.090
Lord Tenchi!

10:46.930 --> 10:47.670
Tenchi?

10:48.090 --> 10:50.720
What are you
doing up there, Tenchi?

10:51.630 --> 10:54.590
Just in time, somehow!

10:58.800 --> 11:00.090
There's a problem
in the past!

11:00.340 --> 11:01.170
What?

11:01.550 --> 11:03.420
And there's the proof!

11:06.420 --> 11:07.250
Check this out.

11:07.510 --> 11:08.760
Huh?

11:15.930 --> 11:19.250
She's not there!
Tenchi's mother has disappeared!

11:20.210 --> 11:23.300
Yeah! And here,
and here, too.

11:24.630 --> 11:26.630
Washu, what's going on?

11:47.670 --> 11:49.670
26 years ago...

11:50.090 --> 11:53.170
something happened to
Lord Tenchi's mother and...

11:53.250 --> 11:55.840
as a result,
the Masaki family died out.

11:57.170 --> 12:00.510
Lord Tenchi has never
been born into this world.

12:00.760 --> 12:03.460
But nothing's
happened to us.

12:03.590 --> 12:06.380
There is only one person
in the whole universe...

12:06.420 --> 12:08.760
who has the ability to interfere
in time and space...

12:08.970 --> 12:11.970
and that is me, this Washu.

12:15.170 --> 12:17.760
From time to time,
I've been able to catch...

12:17.840 --> 12:20.510
sudden misalignments of time factors
in my sub-space laboratory.

12:21.340 --> 12:23.340
There's a sudden shift
in the continuity of history...

12:23.510 --> 12:26.630
centering on the Masaki
family 26 years ago.

12:27.010 --> 12:29.340
If we don't do something,

12:29.420 --> 12:32.550
it won't be just Tenchi's history
that changes, it'll be ours, too.

12:42.510 --> 12:45.050
But they're not yours
to begin with.

12:45.300 --> 12:48.510
So for now, the shield I've
put around Lord Tenchi...

12:48.590 --> 12:50.800
is blocking the time axis...

12:51.510 --> 12:55.010
and so nothing has
happened to you, either.

12:55.090 --> 12:57.380
But it was
the best I could do.

12:57.510 --> 12:58.670
So that means that...

12:58.760 --> 13:00.210
Tenchi.

13:02.840 --> 13:04.010
No way!

13:04.510 --> 13:06.210
But it's a fact.

13:06.300 --> 13:10.210
So then what the hell is it
that happened to Tenchi's mother?

13:10.340 --> 13:13.340
Well,
I haven't got a clue.

13:14.760 --> 13:17.760
So isn't there anything we can
do to help Tenchi? Washu!

13:18.250 --> 13:20.250
Miss Washu...

13:20.340 --> 13:21.720
Miss Washu?

13:26.670 --> 13:29.590
Well, there is a way to help
and only one.

13:30.210 --> 13:31.930
Really? Miss Washu?

13:32.590 --> 13:36.210
First, we go back in time axis
when before Tenchi vanished...

13:36.420 --> 13:41.090
then go back more
to protect Tenchi's mother.

13:47.170 --> 13:51.090
That part-time job of mine.
I'm worn out!

13:52.210 --> 13:53.590
Well, we've got to get going
early tomorrow, too...

13:53.760 --> 13:56.630
so you'd better
get to sleep. Huh?

14:00.880 --> 14:04.720
Yeah, that's one thing you never
have any trouble doing right.

14:22.130 --> 14:23.420
<i>Attention to all GP units.</i>

14:23.510 --> 14:27.130
<i>Kain, who's been</i>
<i>in custody, has escaped...</i>

14:32.460 --> 14:35.970
<i>I wonder what that signal</i>
<i>was all about.</i>

14:40.760 --> 14:42.840
Good evening.

14:43.630 --> 14:44.930
Ryoko?

14:46.050 --> 14:47.840
Hey, I've come to get you.

14:53.340 --> 14:54.510
All right.

14:54.670 --> 14:57.510
I'm going to send you
26 years back in time...

14:57.670 --> 15:00.630
with this time
cause/effect controller...

15:00.720 --> 15:04.300
and I want you to do as I say
when you get back there.

15:04.380 --> 15:07.510
Now, I still don't have
the data together yet...

15:07.670 --> 15:09.630
for exactly
where and what happens...

15:09.720 --> 15:12.300
to Lord Tenchi's mother,
so be careful back there...

15:12.670 --> 15:13.970
and make especially sure...

15:14.050 --> 15:16.010
that you don't come
into contact with her.

15:16.760 --> 15:20.550
The chance of a time paradox
is very, very high.

15:20.880 --> 15:23.010
Hey, hey, are you sure this
is going to be all right?

15:23.090 --> 15:25.380
Nothing ventured,
nothing gained, right?

15:25.550 --> 15:28.050
I hate to put you
to all this trouble...

15:28.170 --> 15:29.050
Yeah, that's great...

15:29.170 --> 15:32.010
but why do we have to
get mixed up in this mess?

15:33.250 --> 15:35.510
I'm getting dizzy.

15:36.380 --> 15:39.050
Anyway, you just make sure
when you get there...

15:39.130 --> 15:40.670
don't do anything stupid.

15:40.720 --> 15:42.380
If history gets
thrown any further off...

15:42.420 --> 15:43.720
it's gonna be
out of my control.

15:43.880 --> 15:46.670
Yeah, yeah. We got it
the first time.

15:46.760 --> 15:49.340
You are the one
I can't trust the most.

15:51.210 --> 15:52.510
Hang on!
We are accelerating.

15:52.590 --> 15:54.050
- What?
- Are you serious?

15:54.670 --> 15:56.460
Hey, wait!

15:56.630 --> 15:58.050
I'm gonna throw up!

15:58.210 --> 16:00.250
Stop this thing, please!

16:00.630 --> 16:02.340
Go!

16:30.210 --> 16:34.420
AUTUMN 1970

16:30.210 --> 16:34.420
Thus began our journey of
26 years back into the past.

16:42.720 --> 16:46.630
Today, we're looking at
'The Demon of the Rashomon'...

16:46.970 --> 16:48.590
the fourth story in the
collection of tales called...

16:48.670 --> 16:50.300
the 'Uji Shui Monogatari'.

16:50.460 --> 16:52.420
This is a story of
a triangular relationship...

16:52.510 --> 16:54.590
between a warrior,
a demon, and a princess...

16:54.670 --> 16:57.300
- Uh, Miss?
- Yes? What is it?

16:57.930 --> 17:00.630
We did that story
yesterday, Miss.

17:00.800 --> 17:06.630
What? Oh, no! That's
the only story I know!

17:06.720 --> 17:08.250
Now what do I do?

17:09.130 --> 17:10.630
That idiot!

17:23.460 --> 17:24.510
Hey, Ayeka...

17:24.590 --> 17:25.340
What?

17:25.510 --> 17:28.170
Amazing, isn't it?
Tenchi's old man over there...

17:28.300 --> 17:31.340
to see him when he's young,
he looks exactly like Tenchi doesn't he?

17:31.590 --> 17:34.760
Well, it's not too late,
you know.

17:34.840 --> 17:37.010
Father is still single,
you know.

17:37.510 --> 17:41.010
What? I'm not talking
about that dirty old man.

17:41.090 --> 17:45.630
I'm talking about Tenchi's father
as we see him in the past.

17:45.720 --> 17:48.670
What the hell
is she talking about?

17:48.760 --> 17:51.010
What are you talking about?

17:51.130 --> 17:53.840
You know what? If Father
never marries Mother...

17:53.930 --> 17:55.930
Tenchi will never
even be born, will he?

17:56.210 --> 17:58.090
I know that!

17:58.170 --> 18:01.670
And just when
did Father and Mother...

18:01.840 --> 18:04.800
become your parents anyway?

18:04.880 --> 18:07.340
Well, we'll just have to let the future
take care of itself, won't we?

18:07.630 --> 18:10.720
Huh! Are you stupid?
It won't happen!

18:10.840 --> 18:15.010
What? I don't wanna be told
by somebody stupid!

18:15.090 --> 18:17.210
What did you say? Huh?

18:24.880 --> 18:26.880
Oh, it's nothing.

18:53.880 --> 18:55.010
Let's begin.

19:03.090 --> 19:04.340
That looks so great on you!

19:04.420 --> 19:06.760
What can I do about it?

19:06.930 --> 19:08.930
I didn't know there'd
be a class like this.

19:09.010 --> 19:12.250
Well, like they said,
you get what you deserve.

19:12.930 --> 19:15.090
Hey, you, listen...

19:18.050 --> 19:21.050
At least I got to borrow
a gym suit from Achika.

19:21.130 --> 19:25.550
But the one you're wearing
is from that gym teacher!

19:27.090 --> 19:29.800
I don't know
the whole story...

19:29.930 --> 19:33.130
but the word is that he has some
sort of medical ailment...

19:33.300 --> 19:35.090
particular to men.
So there!

19:35.300 --> 19:36.720
Yuck!

19:41.840 --> 19:45.720
Huh? What's the matter,
you two transfers?

19:46.420 --> 19:48.460
<i>Oh, he's... scratching down there.</i>

19:53.380 --> 19:54.880
Hey! Give me yours!

19:54.970 --> 19:56.380
No way!

19:56.460 --> 19:57.630
Take it off! Right now!

19:57.720 --> 19:59.460
Ah, what are you doing?

19:59.630 --> 20:03.630
Cut it out!
Leave me alone!

20:04.250 --> 20:05.460
What? Hey! Stop that!
Both of you!

20:05.630 --> 20:06.800
You keep out of this!

20:06.970 --> 20:09.340
That's no way to
talk to your teacher!

20:09.510 --> 20:11.670
Look, those two fighting again.

20:21.880 --> 20:22.760
Here.

20:23.010 --> 20:28.170
Thank you, but
what are you doing here?

20:28.300 --> 20:30.170
Waiting for my big sister.

20:30.300 --> 20:31.590
Your big sister?

20:32.130 --> 20:33.130
Uh-huh.

20:49.670 --> 20:51.010
Achika!

20:52.590 --> 20:55.010
Uh, coming!

20:55.970 --> 20:56.720
Thanks again.

20:56.800 --> 20:57.970
Bye-bye.

21:02.550 --> 21:04.720
Wow! That was close!

21:04.930 --> 21:07.380
Yeah. Miss Washu
is going to be angry.

21:07.460 --> 21:11.050
I knew I was
coming back to the past...

21:11.380 --> 21:15.050
but when I think of her
as my mother, I get excited.

21:15.550 --> 21:17.210
Tenchi.

21:18.720 --> 21:21.720
Sasami, don't tell
anyone about this, okay?

21:21.800 --> 21:22.840
Sure!

21:25.720 --> 21:27.460
Ready?

21:34.670 --> 21:35.880
<i>Mother.</i>

22:07.050 --> 22:10.880
I wish I didn't have to
commute such a long distance.

22:16.970 --> 22:18.250
I'm home!

22:25.510 --> 22:28.590
Oh, I'm so hungry!
I'll fix dinner right... huh?

22:32.720 --> 22:33.630
Hi!

22:34.170 --> 22:35.970
Hope we're
not putting you out.

22:36.130 --> 22:38.250
Welcome home.

22:38.460 --> 22:42.420
Father, these people,
what are they doing here?

22:42.510 --> 22:45.590
Yes, the school called.

22:45.670 --> 22:50.050
This is Ayeka and Ryoko.
We're going to be looking after them.

22:50.300 --> 22:55.460
We are? They just changed schools
today. They're in my class.

22:55.550 --> 22:59.010
Yes, apparently, they live such
a long way from the school...

22:59.130 --> 23:01.170
that it's hard
for them to commute.

23:01.300 --> 23:05.170
- I'm very happy to be here.
- Yeah, glad to be here.

23:05.250 --> 23:06.340
Uh, well, happy
to have you here.

23:06.760 --> 23:09.170
Well, that's wonderful.

23:09.250 --> 23:12.510
You've had a very
lonely time of it...

23:12.590 --> 23:15.170
since your mother died.

23:19.840 --> 23:24.090
Hey, I'm starving!
Is dinner ready yet?

23:24.250 --> 23:25.970
It'll be ready in a minute.

23:26.510 --> 23:29.250
Why don't you
help out a little?

23:29.340 --> 23:32.340
Oh, yeah? I don't
see you doing anything?

23:32.460 --> 23:36.340
- How dare you speak to me like that?
- Oh, don't start again, you two.

23:37.170 --> 23:38.800
Uh? Who could that be?

23:39.250 --> 23:41.550
Good evening.

23:43.510 --> 23:45.010
Miss Mihoshi!

23:45.090 --> 23:47.460
Well... let's see.

23:47.840 --> 23:51.210
I'm conducting a home visit.

23:51.300 --> 23:53.300
A home visit?

23:54.590 --> 23:58.720
Nobody makes home visits
at this hour!

23:59.010 --> 24:00.050
That fool!

24:00.130 --> 24:03.550
I told her to go and take a look
without making anyone suspicious!

24:04.630 --> 24:08.720
Oh, good. It looks like she's
managed to get into the house.

24:11.010 --> 24:13.550
Bon appétit!

24:13.670 --> 24:17.050
- This is so good!
- Everything is great!

24:18.550 --> 24:21.170
Just what is
going on here, I wonder?

24:24.130 --> 24:26.880
You all did a great job
of getting into the house...

24:26.970 --> 24:29.880
without Grandpa realizing
anything was going on.

24:32.010 --> 24:35.380
Well, just a little bit of this perfume...
I borrowed from Miss Washu.

24:35.460 --> 24:37.930
Being sneaky
comes naturally, huh?

24:38.720 --> 24:39.760
What do you mean?

24:40.250 --> 24:41.510
All right, all right.

24:41.590 --> 24:46.720
Anyway, we've managed to all
get safely back here to 1970.

24:47.550 --> 24:50.760
But how can we possibly
save Tenchi's mother...

24:50.880 --> 24:53.420
when we don't know
the danger she faces?

24:55.130 --> 25:00.250
Ah! Here it is!
A message is coming!

25:08.300 --> 25:10.300
<i>So, it looks like you</i>
<i>all got there safely.</i>

25:10.970 --> 25:12.550
Got here safely?
What do you mean?

25:13.130 --> 25:17.130
<i>Well, this time travel by fixing</i>
<i>the position of the time axis...</i>

25:17.250 --> 25:19.630
<i>was more difficult</i>
<i>than I thought.</i>

25:19.720 --> 25:24.130
<i>I wasn't 100% sure it was even</i>
<i>going to work, actually.</i>

25:24.210 --> 25:26.130
What?

25:27.050 --> 25:29.300
So you mean if
you'd put a foot wrong...

25:29.420 --> 25:32.930
we'd have ended up wandering
around time forever?

25:33.010 --> 25:35.090
That'd have been awful!

25:35.170 --> 25:37.090
Damn it, Washu!

25:37.300 --> 25:39.460
<i>All right!</i>
<i>The important thing is that...</i>

25:39.550 --> 25:41.760
<i>you've gotten to where</i>
<i>you're supposed to be.</i>

25:45.840 --> 25:49.340
Um, Miss Washu,
I'd like you to tell me...

25:49.510 --> 25:53.010
exactly when and where my
mother's going to disappear.

25:54.010 --> 25:55.800
<i>It is...</i>

26:04.930 --> 26:08.250
Achika! I've come to
give this back to you.

26:08.340 --> 26:10.670
Tanaka! I haven't
seen you for days!

26:11.300 --> 26:12.840
How's your cold?

26:12.970 --> 26:14.340
Oh, my throat's
still kind of sore...

26:14.420 --> 26:17.840
but I've got a test coming up.
So, what can I do?

26:17.930 --> 26:20.090
Achika, are you
listening to me?

26:20.170 --> 26:21.420
Uh, yes, I'm coming.

26:21.510 --> 26:25.720
This magazine was really interesting
especially Goro, who looks great.

26:25.880 --> 26:27.170
Um? Which one?

26:27.250 --> 26:28.880
Michiru was good, too.

26:29.210 --> 26:30.460
Oh, this feature, huh?

26:30.550 --> 26:33.210
I read this section
many times myself.

26:42.380 --> 26:46.720
<i>Achika's point</i>
<i>of disappearance...</i>

26:46.840 --> 26:50.380
<i>is sometime within</i>
<i>the next 7 days.</i>

27:03.970 --> 27:09.420
<i>And, Kiyone, I've confirmed</i>
<i>GP Headquarter's disappearance.</i>

27:12.800 --> 27:15.760
<i>Their last transmission</i>
<i>mentioned Kain.</i>

27:19.170 --> 27:20.340
Here it comes!

27:20.420 --> 27:21.510
Uh? Whoa!

27:24.090 --> 27:26.840
All right! 1 down.

27:31.210 --> 27:33.420
Come and get me,
if you dare!

27:33.510 --> 27:35.250
She really
gets on my nerves.

27:40.510 --> 27:44.090
<i>Lord Tenchi, shield energy lasts...</i>

27:44.250 --> 27:47.760
<i>only 7 days more. Be careful.</i>

28:00.460 --> 28:03.880
Have you
noticed any changes?

28:04.970 --> 28:06.300
Uh...

28:06.420 --> 28:09.130
Anything, no matter how
trivial it might seem.

28:09.250 --> 28:11.090
Huh! I have something!

28:11.170 --> 28:11.970
Huh? What is it?

28:12.300 --> 28:13.930
You know, at lunch...

28:14.010 --> 28:15.970
they serve
the fried-noodle bread...

28:16.090 --> 28:18.630
which usually is the first
thing to be sold out...

28:18.720 --> 28:21.460
but today there
were 3 pieces left.

28:21.550 --> 28:23.800
I think that's
an emergency, don't you?

28:23.880 --> 28:25.460
Oh, really?

28:25.590 --> 28:29.130
Well, let's leave aside the
stupidity we expect from you.

28:31.340 --> 28:34.090
At any rate, it is certain...

28:34.170 --> 28:38.420
that something is going to
happen to Achika, isn't it?

28:42.670 --> 28:43.510
Lord Tenchi!

28:43.590 --> 28:45.170
Tenchi, what's wrong?

28:47.630 --> 28:48.970
He's disappearing!

28:49.050 --> 28:50.340
Oh, no!

28:50.420 --> 28:52.670
I hope Achika is okay.

28:53.340 --> 28:56.970
Hey, wait a minute! We're
all here, and that means...

28:57.050 --> 28:58.340
Mother?

28:58.460 --> 29:00.840
No one is watching her!

29:01.010 --> 29:03.970
Sasami, you take care
of Tenchi!

29:04.050 --> 29:04.840
Right!

29:05.760 --> 29:08.840
Hurry, everyone!
Let's split up and look for her!

29:14.720 --> 29:16.380
Mother.

29:22.210 --> 29:28.380
Achika!
Achika, where are you? Achika?

29:35.630 --> 29:37.380
Hey! Achika!

29:37.670 --> 29:39.380
Achika!

29:39.670 --> 29:41.050
Achika?

29:41.420 --> 29:42.210
Achika?

29:43.050 --> 29:45.300
Please! Answer me!

29:45.970 --> 29:47.670
Hey! Did you find her?

29:47.760 --> 29:49.550
No. How about you?

29:49.720 --> 29:50.840
No, I couldn't
find her either.

29:50.930 --> 29:53.010
Let's check on Tenchi.

29:54.590 --> 29:57.340
Well, it seems okay.

29:57.420 --> 29:58.760
- Well.
- You did it again?

29:59.880 --> 30:02.880
I'm really sorry for
all this trouble.

30:02.970 --> 30:04.250
Ah, Ryo-ohki?

30:09.340 --> 30:10.420
Ryo-ohki?

30:10.550 --> 30:11.420
What is it?

30:16.010 --> 30:17.380
Maybe it's...

30:17.460 --> 30:18.250
Mother.

30:18.420 --> 30:19.880
Let's go!

30:36.930 --> 30:38.720
Nobuyuki!

30:39.170 --> 30:40.800
Oh, Achika.

30:40.880 --> 30:44.970
You're on cleanup today, aren't you?
What are you doing way up here?

30:45.130 --> 30:47.880
Hey, what are you drawing?

30:47.970 --> 30:49.970
It doesn't matter.

30:52.050 --> 30:53.420
Well...

30:53.510 --> 30:55.800
Please, show me.
Show me. Show me.

30:59.880 --> 31:00.970
What's this?

31:01.760 --> 31:02.630
It's a house.

31:02.800 --> 31:03.930
A house?

31:04.970 --> 31:06.460
Well, I-I love...

31:06.800 --> 31:08.210
Yes?

31:09.300 --> 31:15.300
I love to imagine and draw
different houses like this.

31:17.010 --> 31:18.670
What's wrong with you?

31:20.670 --> 31:22.460
Oh, uh, it's nothing.

31:22.550 --> 31:24.590
Can I have the book?

31:26.010 --> 31:30.010
Uh, you know, a window might
be nice here by the roof don't you think?

31:30.170 --> 31:31.460
What?

31:37.250 --> 31:38.510
Like this?

31:38.800 --> 31:43.340
Well, more like that.

31:43.930 --> 31:47.670
Hey, you've got
good taste, Achika.

31:47.760 --> 31:49.170
You really think so?

31:49.250 --> 31:49.840
Yeah.

31:50.840 --> 31:54.130
Listen, if you ever manage
to build this house...

31:54.210 --> 31:55.670
can you show me?

31:55.840 --> 31:57.840
What?

31:58.010 --> 31:59.840
Come on.
What's the matter?

31:59.930 --> 32:03.050
Uh, well, okay, I guess.

32:08.670 --> 32:11.300
Are you sure,
is this where she is?

32:11.590 --> 32:13.010
Huh?

32:16.590 --> 32:19.210
There they are!

32:19.880 --> 32:23.510
Having fun all by themselves,
oblivious to everyone.

32:23.590 --> 32:25.050
- Oh, how sweet.
- What?

32:25.210 --> 32:28.210
Hmph! They're
just having fun, huh?

32:31.880 --> 32:33.840
What's the matter?

32:34.050 --> 32:35.050
Nothing.

32:43.340 --> 32:46.090
Oh, come on!

32:46.970 --> 32:49.930
So if Lady Achika
is going to disappear...

32:50.050 --> 32:52.510
because of all these
undefined elements...

32:52.590 --> 32:54.840
if I can just manage
to define them...

32:54.880 --> 32:58.050
I should be able to specify
the prediction range...

32:58.090 --> 33:00.550
for the day she vanishes.

33:05.590 --> 33:07.590
But what are these
undefined elements?

33:09.460 --> 33:14.760
What? A school study trip?

33:21.250 --> 33:23.720
When? When do we leave?

33:24.130 --> 33:26.630
What are you talking about?

33:26.800 --> 33:30.130
Tomorrow, of course.
That's why we divided into groups.

33:30.300 --> 33:31.380
Huh?

34:15.170 --> 34:16.800
Ah, this is so great.

34:16.880 --> 34:19.340
So what are we going to do,
Kiyone?

34:19.420 --> 34:20.840
What are we going to do?

34:21.010 --> 34:22.760
All we can do
is go on this trip together.

34:22.840 --> 34:24.670
I hope I don't get lost.

34:24.760 --> 34:27.340
There are so many people
in Tokyo.

34:27.720 --> 34:31.340
Listen, you're supposed to be a
detective in the Galaxy Police.

34:34.340 --> 34:38.090
What? Kiyone?

34:39.840 --> 34:41.670
Did you fall asleep?

34:47.340 --> 34:51.380
Oh, dear! Have I chosen
a bad time to bring you back?

34:52.380 --> 34:56.840
Miss Washu! If you're
going to bring me back...

34:56.930 --> 35:00.050
please tell me first.

35:00.630 --> 35:03.210
All right. I got it. I got it.

35:06.800 --> 35:10.720
Actually, there's something
I want you to check for me.

35:11.550 --> 35:13.460
What's happened, anyway?

35:14.250 --> 35:16.340
Well, when I convert
the amount of energy...

35:16.420 --> 35:19.050
at the point of
Achika's disappearance...

35:19.130 --> 35:21.050
it correlates exactly...

35:21.170 --> 35:26.050
with the amount developed
when GPHQ vanished.

35:27.760 --> 35:29.090
What? Galaxy Police?

35:29.630 --> 35:32.010
Yes, and because it
disappeared...

35:32.090 --> 35:36.250
right after that last
Kain transmission of yours...

35:36.340 --> 35:40.090
I suspect that there's some
connection between the two.

35:41.800 --> 35:44.170
Can you access
Yagami's computer database?

35:44.590 --> 35:45.760
Of course I can.

35:45.840 --> 35:49.840
I could even get into the account
books of the Science Academy.

36:00.550 --> 36:04.090
Kain. Kain. I'm sure
I've seen that name...

36:04.210 --> 36:08.760
on the list of super A-class
criminals before.

36:11.630 --> 36:12.630
There it is!

36:13.050 --> 36:17.300
Age, gender, origin, history,
all unknown.

36:17.380 --> 36:19.630
Distinguishing
characteristics... none.

36:19.800 --> 36:24.050
Offender number 070669,
rank 'A.'

36:24.630 --> 36:27.460
Universal era 507410...

36:27.630 --> 36:30.300
Characteristic energy form
classified as NVO...

36:30.460 --> 36:34.460
code-name K-A-I-N, Kain...

36:34.840 --> 36:37.970
wanted for destruction of
planets, suspicion of murder...

36:38.050 --> 36:39.720
general warrant issued...

36:39.800 --> 36:43.050
destroyed 13 federated planets
and 275,000 spacecraft...

36:43.130 --> 36:46.800
before he was apprehended
and confined...

36:46.970 --> 36:50.970
in the Galaxy Police
Sub-space Network.

36:51.050 --> 36:53.170
Considered to have the power
to overcome...

36:53.300 --> 36:56.340
even a large force
of Galaxy Police.

36:56.510 --> 36:59.590
Has been confined in the
headquarters sub-space room...

36:59.670 --> 37:02.090
for the past 100 years.

37:10.760 --> 37:13.340
Hm... it's quite beyond Ryoko.

37:13.510 --> 37:15.840
More like a living
brand-new supernova.

37:16.300 --> 37:19.460
But, Miss Washu, even if he
escaped the sub-space room...

37:19.550 --> 37:22.090
how could he go back 26 years in time
and interfere with events there?

37:22.170 --> 37:26.130
Oh, if he could get out
of sub-space...

37:26.210 --> 37:28.840
he wouldn't have any problem
influencing the passage of time.

37:29.340 --> 37:33.630
Assuming Kain for some reason
intends to attack Achika...

37:33.720 --> 37:36.170
the dates that
will happen will be...

37:36.250 --> 37:43.050
between the days of
November 25 and 28, 1970.

37:43.130 --> 37:47.010
The probability is
87% for these 4 days...

37:47.090 --> 37:48.380
and the place will be...

37:48.550 --> 37:50.170
Tokyo!

37:53.720 --> 37:57.380
<i>And we all headed for Tokyo.</i>

37:58.800 --> 38:03.300
He doesn't have to attack us
in the middle of a school trip.

38:03.720 --> 38:07.970
Well, it's not 100%, but that is
the highest probability so far.

38:08.050 --> 38:11.880
This Kain is strong enough to
destroy the entire headquarters?

38:11.970 --> 38:15.050
Come on, Kiyone,
let's go home. Ah?

38:15.130 --> 38:16.250
What are you saying?

38:16.420 --> 38:19.340
What happens if there isn't anyone
willing to protect mother?

38:19.420 --> 38:21.930
We have a mission
to return Lord Tenchi...

38:22.050 --> 38:24.930
to his original state
by protecting her.

38:25.250 --> 38:26.420
Miss Ayeka...

38:26.930 --> 38:31.590
Since when
is Achika your mother...

38:31.760 --> 38:35.590
I'd like to know.
Heh Heh. I know.

38:35.720 --> 38:38.050
Score some points
with Tenchi's mother?

38:38.130 --> 38:41.170
That's your scheme, isn't it?

38:41.720 --> 38:46.720
Don't say such a silly thing.
Your brains must be rotten, huh?

38:46.800 --> 38:49.720
Oh, she's getting mad.
The truth hurts, doesn't it.

38:49.800 --> 38:51.090
You think I didn't see you
yesterday...

38:51.170 --> 38:53.210
sneaking off to Achika
and spending all that time...

38:53.300 --> 38:55.340
talking about what kind
of boys you two like?

38:55.460 --> 38:57.970
Grr. That's not true, Ryoko,
and you know it.

38:58.090 --> 38:59.970
What, you want a fight?

39:00.130 --> 39:01.550
Stop it, please, both of you!

39:01.880 --> 39:04.590
- Ayeka, calm down... please.
- Ow! Let go of me, please!

39:04.670 --> 39:06.460
Ryoko, I'm telling you, this
time I am not letting it pass.

39:06.670 --> 39:10.300
Hmph! Yeah, right,
you stinking sneak.

39:18.050 --> 39:20.460
Please stop it!

39:39.340 --> 39:41.510
<i>Tokyo, Tokyo.</i>

39:42.340 --> 39:44.340
<i>We apologize for the long delay</i>
<i>in reaching our destination.</i>

39:44.510 --> 39:46.800
<i>The AMS was turned on,</i>
<i>which resulted in this delay.</i>

39:46.880 --> 39:48.340
<i>We offer our most humble apologies...</i>

39:48.420 --> 39:50.420
<i>for any inconvenience</i>
<i>you may have been caused.</i>

39:50.510 --> 39:52.170
Finally! We made it!

39:52.250 --> 39:54.010
Yeah, we were supposed
to get here in the evening...

39:54.130 --> 39:55.930
but it's the middle
of the night already.

39:56.210 --> 40:00.930
Third-year Class 2...
is everyone here?

40:01.010 --> 40:03.590
All right, we're leaving.

40:04.670 --> 40:06.010
So who keeps watch tonight?

40:06.170 --> 40:09.130
Somehow I have the feeling
it's going to be us.

40:28.550 --> 40:32.380
Oh, I'm so sleepy! Ah?

40:32.880 --> 40:35.050
Hey! Nobuyuki?

40:36.880 --> 40:38.800
What are you doing?

40:38.880 --> 40:41.720
It'll be a great souvenir.

40:42.010 --> 40:43.050
Oh, you!

40:43.630 --> 40:44.720
Did you sleep well last night?

40:44.840 --> 40:46.210
No, not at all.

40:46.340 --> 40:49.630
Oh, please! It's still too early
in the morning for this.

40:49.720 --> 40:52.130
Yep. They seem to be getting
along just fine.

40:52.210 --> 40:55.800
And we are very tired
from guarding her all night.

40:59.340 --> 41:03.090
It's so hot down here!
Are we leaving yet?

41:03.210 --> 41:05.340
I'm thirsty!

41:07.090 --> 41:12.050
Ah, ah. Good morning,
everybody.

41:12.130 --> 41:14.590
Did you all manage to get
a good night's sleep?

41:14.970 --> 41:16.880
We didn't.

41:19.930 --> 41:21.340
Little brats!

41:54.550 --> 41:59.250
Huh? Oh, come on, you again?
What are you shooting me for?

41:59.340 --> 42:00.630
A record of memories.

42:00.720 --> 42:04.970
Now I've got a question for you.
Are you enjoying this trip?

42:05.460 --> 42:09.970
Yes, I am, but there's one thing
I'm worried about.

42:10.250 --> 42:10.970
Huh?

42:11.050 --> 42:14.210
I wonder if my father
is eating properly.

42:14.300 --> 42:16.800
Oh, that? Don't worry.

42:16.970 --> 42:19.250
People don't die just because
they skip meals for 3 days.

42:20.210 --> 42:20.970
Are you sure?

42:21.090 --> 42:22.300
Probably.

42:25.880 --> 42:27.170
I've got another question.

42:27.550 --> 42:29.340
Okay. Go ahead.

42:29.460 --> 42:32.460
What do you want to be
when you grow up?

42:33.380 --> 42:35.670
Maybe a bride?

42:38.800 --> 42:42.420
Whew! Getting hot and heavy,
aren't you, you two?

42:43.010 --> 42:46.340
What are you implying?
We were just talking.

42:46.630 --> 42:47.840
Whew! Whew!

42:48.010 --> 42:50.340
You don't have to be so shy.

42:50.760 --> 42:53.010
What are you talking about?

42:53.090 --> 42:55.010
Nobuyuki,
why don't you say something?

42:58.170 --> 43:02.090
Look at him!
He's getting so stiff.

43:02.170 --> 43:03.840
I suppose he's on the shy side.

43:04.840 --> 43:07.380
What are those idiots doing?

43:07.880 --> 43:11.050
Yes, just when your mother
and father...

43:11.130 --> 43:14.050
are starting to get along
so well together.

43:16.090 --> 43:18.380
Huh? Ah, Tenchi!

43:22.300 --> 43:25.050
Whew! Just in time!

43:27.010 --> 43:29.510
Thanks, Sasami.

43:30.090 --> 43:34.840
I wonder if Miss Washu's
shield is losing strength.

43:35.550 --> 43:36.550
Yeah.

43:42.380 --> 43:45.010
How am I going to manage to look
after my mother like this?

43:45.760 --> 43:47.380
Tenchi.

43:49.720 --> 43:53.550
Oh, here you are!
Come on, you two, come out.

43:53.630 --> 43:56.250
No one's going to see you
with all these students around.

43:56.340 --> 43:57.090
Ryoko.

43:57.170 --> 44:00.590
Ryoko, Tenchi was about
to disappear again.

44:00.670 --> 44:01.420
Really?

44:15.460 --> 44:17.050
That's the guy!

44:21.720 --> 44:23.670
That bastard!

44:26.300 --> 44:27.590
Hey! Hold it right there!

44:30.510 --> 44:31.630
Damn!

44:38.720 --> 44:41.460
That bastard!
He's mocking me.

44:54.670 --> 44:57.090
Some of this
millet and rice cake, please.

44:57.510 --> 44:59.720
Hey! One of those
sweet bean paste doll cakes!

45:00.050 --> 45:02.630
I'll have a fan, please.

45:15.760 --> 45:17.460
Yeah, it's good, huh?

45:26.090 --> 45:28.010
Did that guy say something
to you?

45:28.170 --> 45:29.760
No, nothing. Why?

45:29.840 --> 45:31.590
Here. You can have this.

45:31.930 --> 45:35.170
Was that guy her type,
I wonder?

45:55.010 --> 45:57.380
Damn! Where did he go?

46:12.250 --> 46:14.130
Put your hands
behind your head.

46:20.210 --> 46:24.380
Who are you? Why are you
following Achika around?

46:24.550 --> 46:29.340
Serious offender, case number
80812029, if I'm not mistaken.

46:29.420 --> 46:32.550
You must be the space pirate
Ryoko, I presume.

46:32.670 --> 46:37.250
You're from the Galaxy Police?
Are you with Kiyone and Mihoshi?

46:37.420 --> 46:42.590
You seem to be getting along well
with those first-class detectives.

46:43.550 --> 46:46.250
I am a special operative
with the Galaxy Police...

46:46.420 --> 46:48.590
dealing with serious criminals.

46:48.760 --> 46:52.590
The energy of the fugitive Kain
has drawn me to this era.

46:55.210 --> 46:59.010
Kain? Just who is
this Kain, anyway?

46:59.090 --> 47:01.420
And what's he got to do
with Achika?

47:01.590 --> 47:05.420
Kain is a being who hates
the House of Jurai.

47:06.420 --> 47:08.090
A hundred years ago...

47:08.250 --> 47:10.590
after he went on a rampage
of murder and destruction...

47:10.760 --> 47:13.590
across the known universe...
the Emperor Jurai...

47:13.760 --> 47:17.420
cooperated with the Galaxy
Police in capturing him.

47:26.050 --> 47:30.460
Then a week ago, he made
the GPHQ vanish and escaped...

47:31.210 --> 47:33.130
and he's come to this world
and time...

47:33.210 --> 47:36.130
to take revenge
and swallow up the Jurai.

47:36.670 --> 47:38.460
But that doesn't have anything
to do with Achika!

47:38.630 --> 47:40.970
Yes, it does.
The current Jurai Emperor...

47:41.050 --> 47:43.720
has nothing to do with his captivity
but Kain hates his guts.

47:44.460 --> 47:47.380
Kain lives on anti-Jurai energy.

47:47.550 --> 47:52.050
So he's out to revenge himself on anyone
who has that opposing energy.

47:53.590 --> 47:57.460
So, of course, Yosho and Lady
Achika are some of those people.

47:59.010 --> 48:01.630
So she's like an innocent
bystander.

48:08.970 --> 48:10.840
Take this!

48:17.300 --> 48:18.340
That bastard!

48:20.300 --> 48:21.800
Definitely the work of
the serious offender Ryoko.

48:21.880 --> 48:23.170
You're very good, you know.

48:23.300 --> 48:26.340
I don't know why all of you
have come to this era...

48:28.510 --> 48:29.930
but I'll tell you this.
Kain's mine!

48:30.010 --> 48:31.130
Uh? What the...

48:36.050 --> 48:37.010
Wait!

48:38.010 --> 48:41.720
I'll let you run free
until I defeat Kain.

48:45.380 --> 48:46.380
What's he...

48:48.380 --> 48:51.380
And what happens if you get in
the way of them coming together?

48:51.880 --> 48:56.050
If my mother and father
don't marry, I don't get born!

48:56.210 --> 48:59.970
So, do me a favor and stop
meddling with them, will you?

49:01.050 --> 49:02.050
I'm sorry.

49:02.210 --> 49:05.720
We didn't mean
anything by it, honest.

49:06.380 --> 49:10.010
Anyway, I think I know
what Kain is after.

49:10.090 --> 49:10.880
What did you say?

49:11.550 --> 49:13.880
Kiyone! Let's go buy
some souvenirs!

49:14.550 --> 49:18.210
There's a souvenir shop
on the first floor of the hotel.

49:18.380 --> 49:21.090
What, are you all coming?

49:22.420 --> 49:24.840
Mihoshi, where's Achika?

49:25.630 --> 49:27.930
Well, let's see.

49:28.090 --> 49:30.050
We were together
as far as the bath.

49:30.130 --> 49:31.250
Oh, no!

49:31.800 --> 49:33.930
I'll go find her.

49:34.010 --> 49:35.720
I'm sorry.

49:37.050 --> 49:40.420
You are one useless character.

49:40.550 --> 49:44.210
I just can't do anything right
without Kiyone.

49:44.300 --> 49:47.250
Speaking of which,
where's Kiyone?

49:47.340 --> 49:52.210
I told her to come
to this room.

49:52.800 --> 49:56.670
Kiyone? Kiyone?

49:57.090 --> 49:59.420
Where are you?

50:00.420 --> 50:01.720
Kiyone?

50:02.720 --> 50:04.630
Kiyone?

50:04.760 --> 50:06.130
Kiyone?

50:06.300 --> 50:09.420
Where has she gone?

50:19.880 --> 50:21.970
What was that?

50:25.300 --> 50:26.250
It's you, Kiyone!

50:26.340 --> 50:28.250
Hey! What happened?

50:28.340 --> 50:30.800
I wish Miss Washu would find
a better landing place...

50:30.970 --> 50:32.420
when she does her
damn time transfers.

50:32.800 --> 50:34.210
Washu did this?

50:34.300 --> 50:36.380
So, all this equipment
is from Washu?

50:37.170 --> 50:41.300
Uh, yeah. She'll explain it
in detail herself.

50:44.880 --> 50:46.670
<i>Hi! How are you all doing?</i>

50:47.170 --> 50:48.590
Miss Washu!

50:48.670 --> 50:50.170
<i>How is everything?</i>
<i>All right?</i>

50:50.300 --> 50:52.340
Yes, so far.

50:52.460 --> 50:54.170
What about Kain?

50:54.250 --> 50:56.340
<i>Yes, what about Kain...</i>

50:56.970 --> 51:00.590
<i>The anti-Jurai energy attack on</i>
<i>Lady Achika will come tomorrow.</i>

51:00.670 --> 51:04.340
<i>I'm just about 99% positive.</i>

51:04.460 --> 51:06.930
<i>The place is somewhere where there's</i>
<i>a tower for electronic waves.</i>

51:07.300 --> 51:09.670
A tower for electronic waves...

51:10.170 --> 51:11.670
The Tokyo Tower!

51:11.840 --> 51:13.460
That's where we're
supposed to go tomorrow!

51:13.550 --> 51:14.630
Oh, no!

51:14.720 --> 51:18.800
Now I won't be able to take a picture
from the observation deck!

51:18.880 --> 51:20.840
- Will you shut up?
- Oh! Ouch!

51:21.010 --> 51:22.010
<i>Listen up!</i>

51:22.170 --> 51:25.250
<i>I have the data from</i>
<i>when Kain was captured...</i>

51:25.340 --> 51:26.800
<i>a hundred years ago.</i>

51:26.880 --> 51:29.510
<i>At that time he was taken</i>
<i>through a combination...</i>

51:29.590 --> 51:31.550
<i>of the sub-space net and the</i>
<i>energy from the Emperor Jurai.</i>

51:36.550 --> 51:38.550
<i>But in this generation...</i>

51:38.930 --> 51:43.050
<i>there is no one alive</i>
<i>who has that amount of energy.</i>

51:43.630 --> 51:45.050
What about Grandpa?

51:45.880 --> 51:49.880
<i>That amount of energy is not</i>
<i>possible even for Lord Katsuhito.</i>

51:50.050 --> 51:51.880
<i>Even if he attained it for a short</i>
<i>time it would be dangerous.</i>

51:52.210 --> 51:53.510
What do you mean?

51:54.340 --> 51:56.460
<i>Two generations before</i>
<i>the Jurai Emperor...</i>

51:56.550 --> 51:59.210
<i>the one who put</i>
<i>the seal on Kain...</i>

51:59.340 --> 52:03.380
<i>died as a result of discharging</i>
<i>that amount of energy.</i>

52:07.720 --> 52:12.590
<i>Now, the Psy-Wave Linkage</i>
<i>equipment I've built...</i>

52:12.800 --> 52:15.720
<i>works by amplifying the</i>
<i>Psy-Wave activity of trees...</i>

52:15.800 --> 52:20.090
<i>and connects it</i>
<i>with the sub-space net.</i>

52:20.550 --> 52:24.090
And? I don't understand
what you're getting at.

52:24.930 --> 52:26.250
<i>What I'm getting at...</i>

52:26.420 --> 52:30.090
<i>is that it combines the Jurai</i>
<i>energy with the sub-space net!</i>

52:30.210 --> 52:32.380
<i>- Kiyone, show it to them.</i>
- Okay.

52:37.930 --> 52:39.930
This is the main booster.

52:40.590 --> 52:42.760
We place this on
the Tokyo Tower.

52:42.880 --> 52:45.170
We put the auxiliary boosters
in 5 other places.

52:45.250 --> 52:47.210
They're activated
by a remote switch.

52:47.300 --> 52:49.050
It'll give us 10 minutes
of power.

52:49.170 --> 52:51.880
10 minutes?
Is that going to be enough?

52:52.420 --> 52:54.050
<i>Look, that's all we can get.</i>

52:54.130 --> 52:56.460
<i>I mean, this is an instant</i>
<i>Jurai energy generator.</i>

52:56.550 --> 52:59.970
<i>Just the fact that it works at</i>
<i>all is better than nothing isn't it?</i>

53:00.170 --> 53:03.720
Can we really generate
Jurai energy here on the Earth?

53:04.250 --> 53:06.460
<i>Well, not just anywhere...</i>

53:06.550 --> 53:08.970
<i>only from the 5 places</i>
<i>on the map I've given Kiyone.</i>

53:09.130 --> 53:11.760
<i>Anywhere other than those places</i>
<i>and it's impossible.</i>

53:12.630 --> 53:14.550
<i>In a way, we're lucky</i>
<i>that the attack...</i>

53:14.630 --> 53:17.130
<i>is going to happen</i>
<i>at the Tokyo Tower.</i>

53:18.300 --> 53:20.420
Meguro, Mejiro.

53:20.510 --> 53:21.760
Hey!

53:22.210 --> 53:24.460
These are the Five-Color
Edo Fudo temples, aren't they?

53:24.590 --> 53:26.970
The Five-Color Fudo?

53:27.840 --> 53:30.590
In feudal times, they put up
statues of Fudo-Muo-o...

53:30.670 --> 53:32.840
to guard the Edo castle here.

53:32.930 --> 53:36.840
The others are the Red Eye,
Blue Eye, and Yellow Eye.

53:36.930 --> 53:37.840
That must be it.

53:38.010 --> 53:39.800
<i>You're right!</i>

53:39.880 --> 53:43.170
<i>The only way to get large</i>
<i>amounts of energy quickly...</i>

53:43.250 --> 53:46.510
<i>is to use the ancient</i>
<i>holy places.</i>

53:46.590 --> 53:47.510
So now we'd better decide...

53:47.670 --> 53:50.340
who's going to go around
to each temple...

53:50.460 --> 53:53.300
and who's going to keep
an eye on Lady Achika.

53:53.880 --> 53:56.340
I'll keep watch on Mother.

53:58.800 --> 54:00.250
Tenchi!

54:00.800 --> 54:04.930
This whole thing is a problem
for my mother and myself.

54:06.090 --> 54:09.590
I feel terrible that you've
all been caught up in it.

54:10.210 --> 54:13.800
But I want the one
who has to...

54:14.420 --> 54:17.840
protect my mother
in the final account to be me.

54:25.840 --> 54:27.670
Right, Tenchi.

54:27.760 --> 54:30.380
Leave the rest up to us.

54:30.670 --> 54:32.210
Ryoko.

54:39.380 --> 54:40.380
Tenchi!

54:40.510 --> 54:41.510
Tenchi?

54:42.630 --> 54:43.300
Tenchi?

54:43.380 --> 54:45.010
Tenchi?

54:50.460 --> 54:53.550
Achika! What's wrong?
What's the matter?

54:53.720 --> 54:56.380
My head...
it's like it's splitting in two.

54:56.460 --> 54:57.760
It hurts.

54:57.880 --> 54:59.840
Lady Achika!
What has happened to you?

54:59.930 --> 55:01.930
She suddenly started
to feel this pain.

55:02.170 --> 55:02.930
Lady Achika.

55:03.970 --> 55:06.090
Let's take her back to her room.

55:06.210 --> 55:07.210
Okay.

55:10.340 --> 55:11.720
Damn!

55:12.340 --> 55:13.930
Tenchi.

55:14.460 --> 55:16.090
Tenchi.

55:16.970 --> 55:20.210
I can handle this, Sasami.

55:41.300 --> 55:42.300
Tenchi.

55:44.010 --> 55:45.800
I'm all right.

55:45.970 --> 55:50.970
If I can't take this much pain
how can I protect my mother?

55:52.630 --> 55:56.800
<i>Well... it'll soon be time.</i>

55:57.130 --> 56:01.630
How can you be so calm, Washu?
Do something!

56:02.130 --> 56:03.380
We've got a problem!

56:03.930 --> 56:05.420
Lady Achika's collapsed!

56:05.590 --> 56:08.250
- What?
- Lady Achika's collapsed?

56:18.380 --> 56:19.630
Nobuyuki.

56:20.380 --> 56:22.340
Do you feel better now,
Achika?

56:22.630 --> 56:25.510
Yes, much better.

56:25.670 --> 56:27.010
Good.

56:27.550 --> 56:29.340
Sorry to have worried you.

56:29.840 --> 56:32.250
Don't worry about me.

56:33.010 --> 56:34.760
Hey, Ayeka.

56:35.880 --> 56:38.010
How is Achika doing?

56:38.460 --> 56:40.590
A slight case of anemia,
they say.

56:40.670 --> 56:43.170
I wonder if Kain
is causing all this.

56:43.340 --> 56:45.300
It has to be.

56:46.380 --> 56:51.670
Washu says it's 100% sure that
Kain will materialize tomorrow.

56:51.970 --> 56:54.340
So she should be all right
at least until then.

56:54.510 --> 56:56.170
Let's think about
how we're going to...

56:56.300 --> 56:58.970
install the equipment
we're going to use to catch him.

56:59.050 --> 57:00.550
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

57:01.800 --> 57:04.210
Tenchi, you'll go to
the Tokyo Tower with Achika...

57:04.380 --> 57:07.720
and take the main booster,
okay?

57:08.510 --> 57:09.550
Yes.

57:12.880 --> 57:15.550
<i>The day came on which</i>
<i>Kain was to appear...</i>

57:15.670 --> 57:19.720
<i>The day my mother and I</i>
<i>will never forget.</i>

57:20.630 --> 57:23.880
Kiyone, I'm on my way
to the Tokyo Tower.

57:24.250 --> 57:27.670
Okay. Remember that
the main booster has to be set...

57:27.760 --> 57:30.720
somewhere in the center
of the observation deck.

57:30.840 --> 57:31.880
Right.

57:31.970 --> 57:34.880
As soon as I've got my stuff in position
I'll head straight there as fast as I can.

57:35.010 --> 57:37.130
If there's any problem,
call me on the transceiver.

57:37.210 --> 57:38.050
Yes.

57:39.050 --> 57:40.720
See you then.

57:40.970 --> 57:42.420
Lord Tenchi.

57:43.590 --> 57:44.420
Damn!

57:44.880 --> 57:47.250
If only it was
somewhere I'd been...

57:47.420 --> 57:50.930
then I could just teleport
there and set the thing up.

57:51.010 --> 57:54.420
Right! Just another one of your
many powers that aren't any use.

57:54.590 --> 57:56.050
What did you say?

57:56.130 --> 57:58.930
Come on, you two.
We don't have any time to waste.

57:59.090 --> 58:00.170
Yeah, you're right.

58:00.250 --> 58:02.340
- Let's go.
- Okay!

58:02.460 --> 58:04.420
We should take
the Yamanote line, right?

58:04.510 --> 58:06.380
I'm taking the one
bound for Shibuya.

58:06.760 --> 58:08.510
Are we going in
the same direction, Sasami?

58:08.590 --> 58:11.090
Yup! I have to switch trains
later to Joban line.

58:11.250 --> 58:12.720
Where's Mihoshi?

58:14.590 --> 58:16.880
Mihoshi?

58:17.050 --> 58:19.420
Where are you? Answer me.

58:26.550 --> 58:29.130
Mmm! This is good!

58:40.300 --> 58:42.300
Wow!

58:43.300 --> 58:46.250
So this is the Tokyo Tower.

59:17.510 --> 59:20.630
Great! Looks like
I made it on time.

59:26.130 --> 59:28.510
<i>'Special observation deck is</i>
<i>closed due to construction...'</i>

59:28.630 --> 59:30.590
<i>'from September 20</i>
<i>to December 15.'</i>

59:49.050 --> 59:52.880
There! Now we've got to get
over to the Red Fudo!

59:59.720 --> 01:00:02.380
Excuse me, I'm coming in.

01:00:04.930 --> 01:00:07.460
May you guard Tenchi well.

01:00:20.170 --> 01:00:22.630
Welcome to Tokyo Tower.

01:00:36.210 --> 01:00:38.250
Right there.

01:00:56.130 --> 01:00:59.090
Red Fudo generator in place!

01:01:06.550 --> 01:01:07.420
Yes.

01:01:07.550 --> 01:01:11.050
<i>Tenchi, the generators</i>
<i>are in place on the 5 Fudo.</i>

01:01:11.130 --> 01:01:12.630
<i>How's the main booster coming?</i>

01:01:13.050 --> 01:01:16.210
I'm really sorry. I'm caught up
in a crowd of students.

01:01:16.300 --> 01:01:18.460
<i>Okay, listen. Make sure</i>
<i>you don't switch it on...</i>

01:01:18.590 --> 01:01:21.050
<i>until you've put it in place</i>
<i>on the observation deck.</i>

01:01:21.130 --> 01:01:23.760
<i>If you do it before that,</i>
<i>it'll start to discharge so be careful.</i>

01:01:23.840 --> 01:01:25.720
Right. Got it.

01:01:34.550 --> 01:01:35.590
Any minute now.

01:01:37.460 --> 01:01:39.250
Thank you for waiting.
Please come inside.

01:01:45.550 --> 01:01:49.420
Tokyo Tower's
height is 333 meters...

01:01:49.510 --> 01:01:53.420
and it is the tallest private tower
for electronic waves in the world.

01:01:53.510 --> 01:01:56.340
In front of us are
the Royal Palace...

01:01:56.420 --> 01:01:58.420
Achika! What's the matter?

01:01:58.880 --> 01:02:00.090
I don't feel good.

01:02:02.420 --> 01:02:05.340
Excuse me!
Let me through!

01:02:18.300 --> 01:02:21.340
Oh, no!
What's going on?

01:02:23.010 --> 01:02:25.090
Achika, are you all right?

01:02:26.170 --> 01:02:27.760
Please remain calm.

01:02:27.840 --> 01:02:29.760
The elevator will resume
ascending shortly.

01:02:29.840 --> 01:02:31.670
Hello? Hello?

01:02:32.380 --> 01:02:33.510
Kain?

01:02:49.760 --> 01:02:52.340
- Oh, what's that?
- It's lightning.

01:03:07.510 --> 01:03:09.380
I can feel it...

01:03:09.760 --> 01:03:11.880
I can feel it...

01:03:11.970 --> 01:03:14.550
The blood of the Jurai!

01:03:40.970 --> 01:03:42.420
You pathetic worm!

01:03:49.090 --> 01:03:50.760
Let's get to the stairs
before he comes back.

01:03:50.840 --> 01:03:51.840
Right!

01:04:05.970 --> 01:04:09.210
A survivor from
the Galaxy Police, hmm?

01:04:09.550 --> 01:04:13.630
What magnificent spirit you've shown
in tracking me all the way here!

01:04:13.970 --> 01:04:18.930
Kain, I'm going to get you
if it's the last thing I do!

01:04:30.630 --> 01:04:35.760
Well, whoever you are,
prepare to regret the day...

01:04:35.800 --> 01:04:38.250
you decided to resist
my power!

01:04:47.630 --> 01:04:49.970
Tenchi! Tenchi!

01:04:50.510 --> 01:04:52.010
This isn't good.

01:04:52.130 --> 01:04:55.420
We can't keep up the power
of the Five-Color Fudo much longer!

01:04:55.840 --> 01:04:57.800
<i>Come on, Tenchi!</i>

01:05:00.380 --> 01:05:01.630
<i>Tenchi.</i>

01:05:21.800 --> 01:05:23.210
The center...

01:05:23.460 --> 01:05:25.210
The center!

01:05:26.510 --> 01:05:28.300
Achika!

01:05:31.930 --> 01:05:32.670
He's coming!

01:05:39.460 --> 01:05:40.800
Achika!

01:05:52.800 --> 01:05:54.210
I feel it...

01:05:54.720 --> 01:05:58.050
Someone from the House of Jurai
is here.

01:05:58.130 --> 01:06:01.550
There is someone here
who holds tremendous power.

01:06:02.670 --> 01:06:05.250
Put this in the middle
of the deck! Go!

01:06:06.420 --> 01:06:08.090
I'm counting on you.

01:06:09.420 --> 01:06:11.420
Hey! What is this?

01:06:16.420 --> 01:06:18.170
This is as far as you go!

01:06:18.800 --> 01:06:22.090
Are you of the House
of Jurai?

01:06:23.880 --> 01:06:27.090
Very interesting. We'll see
how much power you have.

01:06:34.760 --> 01:06:36.250
Come on, Achika! Quick!

01:06:37.010 --> 01:06:38.670
Who is that boy?

01:06:38.760 --> 01:06:41.550
Achika,
it's dangerous here!

01:06:45.590 --> 01:06:48.300
Tenchi... you've started?

01:06:50.800 --> 01:06:52.800
Is this how he wants it?

01:07:03.800 --> 01:07:08.090
This looks like the end
of the House of Jurai.

01:07:09.170 --> 01:07:12.630
I'll eradicate you and put you
out of your misery!

01:07:14.720 --> 01:07:16.970
I won't let you
touch my mother!

01:07:26.460 --> 01:07:27.300
Stop!

01:07:32.250 --> 01:07:33.590
Achika?

01:07:35.670 --> 01:07:37.800
I found!

01:07:38.010 --> 01:07:40.630
It's you. I found you!

01:07:40.670 --> 01:07:44.170
None of the others
were the same!

01:07:44.250 --> 01:07:50.250
I've come all the way to this planet
in the middle of nowhere to destroy you!

01:07:50.930 --> 01:07:52.670
What? And you are?

01:07:53.130 --> 01:07:55.510
I am one who has suffered
grievously...

01:07:55.550 --> 01:07:58.550
from the power
that lies latent in you.

01:08:00.010 --> 01:08:02.760
Push the red button!
Hurry!

01:08:17.090 --> 01:08:18.550
Th-this is...

01:08:58.340 --> 01:08:59.760
Achika!

01:09:05.130 --> 01:09:06.090
Nobuyuki!

01:09:06.590 --> 01:09:09.250
I won't go alone!

01:09:09.380 --> 01:09:11.340
I will take you with me!

01:09:17.550 --> 01:09:18.930
Hang on!

01:09:20.090 --> 01:09:22.420
Don't lose your grip
on Achika!

01:09:38.630 --> 01:09:39.760
Dad!

01:09:40.050 --> 01:09:41.010
Mother!

01:09:42.590 --> 01:09:43.760
Ryoko!

01:09:44.170 --> 01:09:47.250
Let go of me, Ryoko!
That's my mother and father!

01:09:47.300 --> 01:09:49.050
Tenchi, Tenchi...

01:09:51.090 --> 01:09:52.800
They've already
been pulled in.

01:09:52.880 --> 01:09:55.800
Let go!

01:09:55.840 --> 01:09:58.970
Let me go!

01:10:31.010 --> 01:10:36.170
And after the Psy-Wave Linkage
generator worked so well, too!

01:10:38.210 --> 01:10:39.340
<i>I never thought...</i>

01:10:39.340 --> 01:10:42.130
<i>that when we sent Kain</i>
<i>into alternate space/time...</i>

01:10:42.210 --> 01:10:45.170
<i>he'd pull Lady Achika</i>
<i>and Nobuyuki in with him!</i>

01:10:52.880 --> 01:10:56.050
Isn't there... isn't there
something we can do...

01:10:56.170 --> 01:11:00.050
to bring my mother
and father back, Miss Washu?

01:11:01.460 --> 01:11:02.720
<i>I'm afraid not.</i>

01:11:02.880 --> 01:11:06.340
<i>It's nearly impossible to determine</i>
<i>the exact coordinates inside alternate space/time.</i>

01:11:06.420 --> 01:11:09.340
<i>So we have no access.</i>

01:11:10.670 --> 01:11:12.210
No way.

01:11:17.670 --> 01:11:20.880
Miss Washu, there must
be something you can do...

01:11:20.970 --> 01:11:24.210
to bring them back.
Miss Washu.

01:11:25.170 --> 01:11:26.720
Please?

01:11:26.840 --> 01:11:28.550
Please?

01:11:55.930 --> 01:11:57.250
Achika!

01:12:01.460 --> 01:12:04.340
<i>It's a pretty long shot, but...</i>

01:12:04.420 --> 01:12:08.250
<i>we can try to transfer Achika's</i>
<i>brain waves into Tenchi...</i>

01:12:08.380 --> 01:12:11.930
<i>then let Ryoko teleport</i>
<i>to those coordinates.</i>

01:12:12.090 --> 01:12:14.760
<i>Well, what are we waiting for?</i>

01:12:14.880 --> 01:12:16.420
<i>You're forgetting</i>
<i>about one thing.</i>

01:12:16.510 --> 01:12:20.210
<i>Even if this works we'll still have to</i>
<i>face Kain once we get there...</i>

01:12:20.300 --> 01:12:23.460
<i>and he is more powerful</i>
<i>than all of you combined.</i>

01:12:30.420 --> 01:12:32.970
<i>What are we</i>
<i>going to do, then?</i>

01:12:41.930 --> 01:12:45.460
It's quite risky but I'll use
the dimensional cannon.

01:12:46.050 --> 01:12:48.930
The dimensional cannon?

01:12:49.050 --> 01:12:51.800
Miss Washu, wait a minute!
You wouldn't even use that...

01:12:51.930 --> 01:12:55.460
if you wanted to take out a whole planet!
That's for blowing up small galaxies!

01:12:56.250 --> 01:12:58.630
Well, considering
who our opponent is...

01:12:58.800 --> 01:13:00.970
if we don't take this
chance to eliminate him...

01:13:01.050 --> 01:13:02.970
there's no telling when
he'll find his way...

01:13:03.050 --> 01:13:05.510
back out of alternative
space and time again.

01:13:07.930 --> 01:13:11.510
I can't believe we're going to use
a huge weapon like that!

01:13:24.670 --> 01:13:26.510
Can you go any faster,
Ryoko?

01:13:26.590 --> 01:13:27.630
Shut up!

01:13:27.720 --> 01:13:29.510
Normally, we wouldn't even
need your help.

01:13:29.630 --> 01:13:31.460
Tenchi and I alone
could handle this, you know.

01:13:31.550 --> 01:13:35.090
All you have is completely
useless destructive power.

01:13:35.170 --> 01:13:36.300
What?

01:13:36.380 --> 01:13:38.420
If Nobuyuki hadn't been
sucked into sub-space...

01:13:38.510 --> 01:13:41.340
we wouldn't have
needed you anyway.

01:13:41.420 --> 01:13:44.720
Lord Tenchi,
thank heavens you're safe!

01:13:44.800 --> 01:13:47.210
Ayeka, I'm sorry.

01:13:47.380 --> 01:13:52.380
Not at all! For your mother,
I'll go through fire through water.

01:13:52.460 --> 01:13:54.210
Listen to her!

01:13:54.380 --> 01:13:56.800
Washu! Ready to transfer.

01:13:56.880 --> 01:13:58.210
<i>Roger!</i>

01:14:22.590 --> 01:14:23.380
Here it is!

01:14:51.420 --> 01:14:53.930
Dimensional cannon
aimed and ready!

01:14:55.420 --> 01:14:58.670
All right, Washu.
Take control. We're all yours.

01:14:59.090 --> 01:15:02.380
Roger! Ryoko, you teleport
to the place...

01:15:02.460 --> 01:15:05.630
that Tenchi imagines,
all right?

01:15:06.130 --> 01:15:08.130
Okay, okay,
just leave it to me.

01:15:10.210 --> 01:15:12.720
We have the shield
for 198 seconds.

01:15:13.340 --> 01:15:16.050
So make sure you get everything
done within that time.

01:15:17.170 --> 01:15:18.250
Yes!

01:15:37.760 --> 01:15:39.300
Nobuyuki!

01:15:42.550 --> 01:15:44.300
Nobuyuki!

01:15:45.340 --> 01:15:46.670
<i>I promise...</i>

01:15:46.840 --> 01:15:50.090
<i>that you will come</i>
<i>and see the house I build.</i>

01:15:57.380 --> 01:15:58.460
Nobuyuki!

01:16:11.460 --> 01:16:12.670
Nobuyuki!

01:16:15.170 --> 01:16:16.760
Nobuyuki!

01:16:19.840 --> 01:16:21.930
One day...

01:16:22.630 --> 01:16:25.010
we'll build that house...
together.

01:16:25.760 --> 01:16:28.550
Nobuyuki... hang in there.

01:16:32.720 --> 01:16:36.840
Nobuyuki
it'll be all over soon.

01:16:39.460 --> 01:16:41.130
I won't allow it.

01:16:45.420 --> 01:16:48.170
I will never allow you!

01:17:04.670 --> 01:17:07.720
I will never forgive you.

01:17:09.050 --> 01:17:10.380
Never forgive you!

01:17:11.930 --> 01:17:13.210
Tenchi?

01:17:13.420 --> 01:17:14.840
Lord Tenchi?

01:17:16.460 --> 01:17:19.090
I understand.
I can see it.

01:17:19.210 --> 01:17:21.420
I'm coming now!

01:17:22.090 --> 01:17:25.250
Mother!

01:17:41.670 --> 01:17:42.420
Tenchi!

01:17:49.670 --> 01:17:54.300
Pretty good...
but not good enough!

01:18:05.800 --> 01:18:09.300
If I can't destroy you,
I'll absorb you!

01:18:32.630 --> 01:18:33.340
Nobuyuki!

01:18:35.720 --> 01:18:36.670
Nobuyuki!

01:18:41.170 --> 01:18:42.670
Nobuyuki!

01:18:59.760 --> 01:19:01.170
We barely made it, huh?

01:19:01.340 --> 01:19:02.840
Nobuyuki?

01:19:02.930 --> 01:19:04.460
You are...

01:19:09.170 --> 01:19:10.590
Tenchi.

01:19:14.010 --> 01:19:16.210
Two minutes left.
Auto-throttle on.

01:19:17.090 --> 01:19:19.380
First and second
safety locks off.

01:19:20.210 --> 01:19:22.340
The shield
is losing power fast.

01:19:22.420 --> 01:19:24.340
It'll still last a while.

01:19:24.420 --> 01:19:26.010
<i>Any news from Tenchi?</i>

01:19:26.090 --> 01:19:27.380
No, not yet.

01:20:00.510 --> 01:20:01.420
A minute to go.

01:20:02.210 --> 01:20:04.340
Energy level maximum.

01:20:06.250 --> 01:20:08.210
Final safety disengaged.

01:20:08.300 --> 01:20:10.090
Counting down!

01:20:10.210 --> 01:20:12.010
<i>Hurry up</i>
<i>and get back here, Tenchi!</i>

01:20:20.380 --> 01:20:21.050
Tenchi!

01:20:36.050 --> 01:20:40.130
Don't worry about me!
Ryoko, get Mother away!

01:20:40.300 --> 01:20:41.970
Lord Tenchi!

01:20:47.930 --> 01:20:50.460
- There's no more time!
- We're finished?

01:21:08.210 --> 01:21:09.300
Lady Achika?

01:21:09.420 --> 01:21:13.300
She's doing great.
That's Tenchi's mother, all right.

01:21:31.840 --> 01:21:34.840
What's this power?

01:21:35.930 --> 01:21:38.510
What's this power?

01:22:18.840 --> 01:22:20.720
Achika, hurry up!

01:22:20.840 --> 01:22:21.880
Okay.

01:22:22.510 --> 01:22:23.720
Hurry!

01:22:32.340 --> 01:22:36.130
The Jurai will not
escape me!

01:22:36.880 --> 01:22:37.550
Kain!

01:22:37.970 --> 01:22:40.050
- They're back!
- Fire!

01:23:33.050 --> 01:23:35.800
Kain's gone, isn't he?

01:23:39.380 --> 01:23:40.420
Yes.

01:23:41.340 --> 01:23:44.090
We gotta get going, too.

01:23:47.590 --> 01:23:50.300
Take care of Nobuyuki,
all right?

01:23:54.050 --> 01:23:56.130
Where are Sasami
and Mihoshi?

01:23:56.210 --> 01:23:58.800
They were transferred back.

01:23:59.170 --> 01:24:02.630
The Tokyo Tower's a wreck.
Is it going to be all right?

01:24:02.800 --> 01:24:07.170
Washu says the renovations just came
10 years earlier than planned.

01:24:07.340 --> 01:24:10.250
Or we can blame it on some
paranormal phenomenon.

01:24:27.840 --> 01:24:31.760
Both of you take care of Tenchi,
all right?

01:24:32.550 --> 01:24:33.840
- What?
- What?

01:24:34.010 --> 01:24:36.010
So you knew all about us?

01:24:36.630 --> 01:24:39.420
The power of the Jurai
opened my eyes.

01:24:39.510 --> 01:24:40.340
I saw...

01:24:42.340 --> 01:24:45.170
when Tenchi
will need me most...

01:24:45.300 --> 01:24:48.210
I won't be able
to be there with him.

01:24:53.880 --> 01:24:56.210
I almost forgot.

01:24:57.800 --> 01:25:00.170
Where is it?

01:25:00.550 --> 01:25:01.630
Here.

01:25:06.510 --> 01:25:08.050
Now that Kain is gone...

01:25:08.170 --> 01:25:10.380
the time cause/effect rhythm
has returned to normal...

01:25:10.550 --> 01:25:15.010
but we have to erase
your memory of all this.

01:25:16.210 --> 01:25:17.880
I'm sorry.

01:25:28.340 --> 01:25:29.840
- Would you...
- Huh?

01:25:29.880 --> 01:25:32.090
return this to him...

01:25:32.170 --> 01:25:34.760
and tell him it's
a very important thing.

01:25:38.800 --> 01:25:40.420
Lady Achika.

01:25:49.970 --> 01:25:54.210
I will live my life
with Nobuyuki to its fullest.

01:25:56.590 --> 01:25:58.170
That's all that matters.

01:26:00.760 --> 01:26:02.720
Take care of yourself.

01:26:06.510 --> 01:26:07.590
Thank you.

01:26:13.630 --> 01:26:15.550
Having you here...

01:26:16.460 --> 01:26:18.130
was really...

01:26:19.460 --> 01:26:20.970
wonderful.

01:26:43.130 --> 01:26:48.050
<i>And so, the incident that occurred</i>
<i>in my parents' time was resolved.</i>

01:26:48.800 --> 01:26:51.880
<i>My mother lost the power</i>
<i>that Kain so feared...</i>

01:26:51.970 --> 01:26:55.670
<i>and 26 years later,</i>
<i>it was passed to me.</i>

01:26:57.090 --> 01:27:00.420
<i>There is only one thing about</i>
<i>this affair that troubles me...</i>

01:27:01.010 --> 01:27:04.170
<i>the power that my mother displayed</i>
<i>in her fight with Kain...</i>

01:27:04.300 --> 01:27:07.340
<i>was obviously the power</i>
<i>of the House of Jurai...</i>

01:27:07.460 --> 01:27:10.010
<i>and in losing that power...</i>

01:27:10.170 --> 01:27:13.340
<i>her own life may well</i>
<i>have been shortened.</i>

01:27:17.250 --> 01:27:18.670
<i>Ironically...</i>

01:27:18.800 --> 01:27:21.670
<i>the Jurai power she</i>
<i>used to save my life...</i>

01:27:22.510 --> 01:27:26.010
<i>was the power by which</i>
<i>she lived.</i>

01:27:27.460 --> 01:27:29.340
<i>I am aware that the past</i>
<i>cannot be changed...</i>

01:27:30.420 --> 01:27:33.170
<i>but the only thing</i>
<i>that makes me able...</i>

01:27:33.300 --> 01:27:37.510
<i>to accept what came to pass is the fact</i>
<i>that my parents were able to...</i>

01:27:37.590 --> 01:27:40.210
<i>spend their young years</i>
<i>happily together.</i>

01:27:40.340 --> 01:27:45.210
<i>NINE YEARS LATER</i>

01:27:46.010 --> 01:27:48.340
Well, the baby's fine,
fortunately.

01:27:48.420 --> 01:27:51.970
And they say that Achika will be
out of the hospital next week.

01:27:52.050 --> 01:27:53.720
Is that so?

01:27:56.510 --> 01:28:01.050
The company has finally agreed
to let me design a building.

01:28:01.170 --> 01:28:04.340
I guess they're finally
recognizing me.

01:28:04.420 --> 01:28:06.170
Is that so?

01:28:10.420 --> 01:28:12.130
You know, Dad...

01:28:12.210 --> 01:28:16.050
I've been thinking about rebuilding
this house one of these days.

01:28:16.210 --> 01:28:19.250
Really? Is that so?

01:28:23.550 --> 01:28:27.720
I have to hurry up and show Achika
the house I promised her.

01:28:31.010 --> 01:28:32.590
Oh, yes, Dad...

01:28:32.760 --> 01:28:35.880
what should we do about
a name for the baby?

01:28:37.880 --> 01:28:40.250
Yes, indeed.

01:28:44.050 --> 01:28:46.880
<i>'Named... Tenchi'</i>

01:28:47.880 --> 01:28:50.590
Good, good...

01:28:51.550 --> 01:28:53.380
good night...

01:28:53.460 --> 01:28:54.880
Tenchi.

01:29:08.420 --> 01:29:10.720
We're all here.

01:29:12.420 --> 01:29:14.970
All right, everyone smile more!

01:29:15.050 --> 01:29:16.630
That's it!

01:29:23.760 --> 01:29:27.930
<i>I can't wait to see it,</i>
<i>your dream house.</i>

01:29:28.010 --> 01:29:31.970
<i>Our dream is still</i>
<i>pretty much alive even now...</i>

01:29:32.300 --> 01:29:33.460
<i>right, Achika?</i>

01:29:33.630 --> 01:29:34.800
Yes.

01:29:42.300 --> 01:29:47.420
<i>I will live my life</i>
<i>with Nobuyuki to its fullest.</i>

01:29:49.800 --> 01:29:52.010
<i>That's all that matters.</i>

01:30:20.970 --> 01:30:30.210
Come to you across the divide
<i>Looking out a wrinkle in time</i>

01:30:30.880 --> 01:30:40.050
There is nothing less I would do
<i>Than to stand up for truth</i>

01:30:40.170 --> 01:30:44.720
In the cold dark ways
<i>Of this lonely place</i>

01:30:44.880 --> 01:30:50.380
I will warm you, hold you

01:30:50.420 --> 01:30:54.970
A gold shield glistens
<i>And your breath quickens</i>

01:30:55.050 --> 01:30:59.880
I stand close by over you

01:31:01.090 --> 01:31:06.010
Two hands held strong and sure with
<i>The power of one</i>

01:31:06.130 --> 01:31:10.930
Reaching out past the walls
<i>That can hold you</i>

01:31:10.970 --> 01:31:15.930
We are guardians, warriors
<i>Come from somewhere to mind</i>

01:31:16.050 --> 01:31:20.670
What creates you and shapes
<i>The Alchemy of Love</i>

01:31:24.050 --> 01:31:31.840
There is a chain of light
<i>Out across the endless skies</i>

01:31:33.300 --> 01:31:41.510
And I see the energy that
<i>Reflects me in your eyes</i>

01:31:42.300 --> 01:31:51.300
And keeps us both alive
<i>And keeps us both alive</i>

01:31:57.460 --> 01:32:06.210
Evening and the shadows will come
<i>To destroy what we have done</i>

01:32:07.130 --> 01:32:16.130
But always will the power of love
<i>Shine a light bright as the sun</i>

01:32:16.670 --> 01:32:20.880
When the cold dark waves on
<i>The shores break</i>

01:32:20.970 --> 01:32:26.720
